 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The eviction policy is 2Q. It separates first-use entries from reused entries, protecting comparison sheets from one-off screening scans. This accepts extra bookkeeping (two queues and a size split) to keep repeatedly revisited clips warm during long sequential screenings. None of the candidates changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q | LRU, Frequency-based with aging | 2Q protects reused sheets from sequential scan eviction. LRU evicts comparison sheets during long screenings. Aged frequency adds counter maintenance and lags project switches. 2Q keeps all changes inside the preview worker's private cache. |
+
+## 2Q Cache Structure
+
+The private cache maintains two queues with a shared 12 GiB budget:
+
+- **A1in** (new entries): First admission queue. Entries enter here on their first cache admission after a render completes. Capacity target: 25% of budget (3 GiB).
+- **Am** (reused entries): Main queue for entries that have been accessed at least twice. Capacity target: 75% of budget (9 GiB).
+
+On cache hit in A1in: promote the entry to Am (move to head of Am).
+On cache hit in Am: move to head of Am (standard LRU within Am).
+On admission when over budget: evict from A1in tail first; if A1in is at or below its target, evict from Am tail.
+
+The 25/75 split is the initial tuning parameter; it may be adjusted based on observed workload without changing the external interface.
