 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a completed preview is admitted to the cache for the first time, the system SHALL place it in the A1in queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a cached preview in A1in is accessed, the system SHALL promote it to the head of the Am queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a cached preview in Am is accessed, the system SHALL move it to the head of the Am queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When admitting a preview would exceed 12 GiB, the system SHALL evict from the A1in tail first; when A1in is at or below 3 GiB, the system SHALL evict from the Am tail.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: The system SHALL maintain the A1in capacity target at 25% (3 GiB) and Am capacity target at 75% (9 GiB) of the 12 GiB budget.
